{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>So long as all the days of the earth endure, seedtime and harvest, cold and heat, summer and winter, day and night shall not cease.</b> They shall not cease from continuing in that unnatural manner which I assigned to them after the Flood — namely that the sun travels upon an orbit inclined away from the equator, and its inclination is the cause of the variation of all these seasons. For before the Flood the sun's course was always along the equator, and therefore it was then perpetually springtime, and in this there was a general perfection for the elements, the plants, the living creatures, and the length of their days. And He said that this shall endure all the days of the earth, until the blessed El repair the corruption that came upon it in the Flood, as it says: הָאָרֶץ הַחֲדָשָׁה אֲשֶׁר אֲנִי עוֹשֶׂה (Isaiah 66:22). For then He will restore the sun's course to the equator as of old, and there will be a general perfection for the elements, the plants, the living creatures, and the length of their days, as it was before the Flood, as it says: כִּי הַנַּעַר בֶּן מֵאָה שָׁנָה יָמוּת וְהַחוֹטֵא בֶּן מֵאָה שָׁנָה יְקֻלָּל (Isaiah 65:20), and this is what He intended in saying: מוֹצָאֵי בֹקֶר וָעֶרֶב תַּרְנִין (Psalms 65:9)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:33.598313228Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}